---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout slug="snipemaxxer-valorant-mobile-setup">
  <div class="gx-guide smx-guide-refresh">
    <div class="gx-hero smx-hero">
      <p class="gx-hero__kicker">The Valorant setup guide</p>
      <p class="gx-hero__line">
        Read rank, RR, teammates, and skins when the right Riot source returns them — then choose
        <strong>one PC, two PCs, or your phone</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="gx-glance">
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">⌖</span> Read-only Riot context</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">◆</span> Rank + RR</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">◌</span> Teammates + skins</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">▣</span> 1 PC / 2 PC / phone</span>
      </div>

      <div class="smx-signal-row" aria-label="Valorant guide status">
        <span class="smx-signal-row__led" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="smx-signal-row__key">Session desk</span>
        <span class="smx-signal-row__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Read-only Riot path</span>
        <span class="smx-signal-row__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span>Freshness labeled</span>
      </div>

      <div class="smx-lobby-card" aria-label="Visual map of the Valorant session desk">
        <div class="smx-lobby-card__top">
          <span class="smx-terminal-label">Valorant / session desk</span>
          <span class="smx-lobby-card__badge">UI MAP · NOT LIVE DATA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="smx-lobby-card__grid">
          <div class="smx-lobby-card__cell">
            <span>Lobby context</span>
            <strong>Phase / teams / players</strong>
            <small>Appears when Riot returns the fields.</small>
          </div>
          <div class="smx-lobby-card__cell">
            <span>Competitive</span>
            <strong>Rank + RR</strong>
            <small>Live, delayed, or cached status stays visible.</small>
          </div>
          <div class="smx-lobby-card__cell">
            <span>Match desk</span>
            <strong>Reports + vault</strong>
            <small>History, crosshairs, watchlists, and alerts.</small>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="smx-lobby-card__foot">
          <span class="smx-lobby-card__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>Source: signed-in Riot Client on the gaming PC</span>
          <strong>READ-ONLY</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="gx-intro">
      Snipemaxxer’s Valorant side is a <strong>read-only session desk</strong>. It can combine provider-backed
      rank and match history with Riot Client context from the gaming PC, while labeling live, delayed, cached,
      offline, and unavailable states instead of pretending everything is real time.
    </p>

    <div class="gx-callout gx-callout--cyan">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">⚡ Quick answer</p>
      <ul class="gx-mini">
        <li><strong>Single PC:</strong> run Riot Client, Valorant, and Snipemaxxer together on the gaming PC. No phone or second PC is required.</li>
        <li><strong>Two PCs:</strong> keep Riot Client and Valorant on the gaming PC, then use Snipemaxxer’s one-time gaming-PC link for the other screen.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> install the PC companion where Riot Client is running, then open the phone view it creates and use its one-time Phone link.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>What the Valorant side can show</h2>
    <ul class="gx-checks">
      <li><strong>Rank, RR, and peak:</strong> see your competitive context and completed-match history. Provider-backed values can be delayed or cached.</li>
      <li><strong>Current lobby context:</strong> read the current phase, full lobby, team split, and teammate intel when Riot returns those fields.</li>
      <li><strong>Teammate skins:</strong> skin data is conditional. If Riot hides an identity or does not return a skin, Snipemaxxer keeps it unavailable instead of guessing.</li>
      <li><strong>Reports:</strong> completed matches can include map, agent, K/D/A, score, headshots, and additional round fields when the provider includes them.</li>
      <li><strong>Desk tools:</strong> keep friends, personal offers, a local crosshair vault, watchlists, and alerts in the same focused window.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="gx-callout gx-callout--cyan">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">📡 Read the status before the number</p>
      <p>
        “Live” means the current session path answered. “Delayed” or “cached” means the value is useful context,
        not a promise that it changed this second. “Unavailable” is an honest boundary — it is not a reason to
        enter a password or force a lookup.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Choose your setup</h2>
    <div class="smx-route-map" aria-label="Snipemaxxer Valorant setup path">
      <div class="smx-route-map__head">
        <span class="smx-route-map__label">The path</span>
        <span class="smx-route-map__note">One source · three ways to view it</span>
      </div>
      <div class="smx-route-map__track">
        <div class="smx-route-node smx-route-node--source">
          <span class="smx-route-node__tag">01 / SOURCE</span>
          <h3>Riot Client</h3>
          <p>Signed in on the gaming PC where the session lives.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="smx-route-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span>read-only context</span></div>
        <div class="smx-route-node smx-route-node--desk">
          <span class="smx-route-node__tag">02 / DESK</span>
          <h3>Snipemaxxer</h3>
          <p>Labels what is live, delayed, cached, offline, or unavailable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="smx-route-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><span>choose a surface</span></div>
        <div class="smx-route-node smx-route-node--view">
          <span class="smx-route-node__tag">03 / VIEW</span>
          <h3>PC · PC · phone</h3>
          <p>Keep the complete desk or take a quick lobby check with you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gx-steps smx-setup-steps">
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">1</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Single PC: the simplest route</h3>
          <p>
            Download Snipemaxxer from the <a href="/snipemaxxer/">product page</a>, then open Riot Client and
            Valorant on the same gaming PC. Launch Snipemaxxer and use its local, read-only Valorant path. This
            keeps the full lobby, reports, crosshair vault, and alerts at one desk.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">2</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Two PCs: put the viewer where you want it</h3>
          <p>
            Keep Valorant and Riot Client on the gaming PC. Use the one-time gaming-PC link shown by Snipemaxxer
            so its other-PC view can receive the same read-only session context. The second PC is a viewer; it
            does not need your Riot password, and the gaming PC remains the source of the session data.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">3</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Phone: use the companion route</h3>
          <p>
            On the PC where Riot Client is running, open the <a href="/snipemaxxer/">Snipemaxxer product page</a>
            and download Maxxtopia Companion. Open it once, use its one-time Phone link, then open the resulting
            mobile view on your phone at <a href="https://mobile.maxxtopia.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mobile.maxxtopia.com</a>.
            Keep the source PC and Riot Client running for fresh data. The phone is a quick lobby check, not a
            replacement for the full Windows reports desk.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">4</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Use the right surface for the question</h3>
          <p>
            Check the lobby view for phase, team split, teammate context, and returned skins. Open Reports for
            completed-match detail. If the live source is unavailable, use the labeled provider history instead
            of treating an old RR, skin, or lobby value as current.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gx-specs">
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">1 PC</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Lowest setup</div></div>
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">2 PCs</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Separate viewer</div></div>
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">Phone</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Companion view</div></div>
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">Read-only</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Riot path</div></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What not to do</h2>
    <ul class="gx-nope">
      <li><strong>Do not enter your Riot password</strong> into Snipemaxxer, the companion, or a phone page. Pairing is not a Riot sign-in.</li>
      <li><strong>Do not expect phone-only discovery.</strong> The phone view needs the companion on the PC where Riot Client is running.</li>
      <li><strong>Do not treat missing skins or names as a bug by default.</strong> Riot may hide or omit those fields, and the guide should stay honest about that.</li>
      <li><strong>Do not call delayed data live.</strong> Read the freshness label before using RR, match, or lobby information for a decision.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="gx-outro">
      <strong>Bottom line:</strong> use one PC when you want the complete desk, two PCs when you want the viewer
      away from the gaming screen, and the phone companion when you want a quick lobby check in your hand. The
      source stays on the gaming PC, the Riot path stays read-only, and unavailable data stays unavailable.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .smx-guide-refresh {
      --smx-amber: #ffb547;
      --smx-oxide: #ff3f69;
      --smx-cyan: #00d4ff;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-hero {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      padding: 1.65rem;
      border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--smx-amber) 68%, transparent);
      background:
        linear-gradient(135deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--smx-amber) 12%, transparent), transparent 43%),
        radial-gradient(100% 120% at 100% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--smx-oxide) 13%, transparent), transparent 62%),
        #ffffff05;
      box-shadow: 0 1.25rem 4rem #0000002e, 0 0 0 1px #ffb5470b;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-hero::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      right: 8%;
      width: 42%;
      height: 2px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--smx-amber), var(--smx-oxide), transparent);
      opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-hero > * {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-hero__kicker {
      color: var(--smx-amber);
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-hero__line strong {
      color: #ffd58e;
      text-shadow: 0 0 1.25rem #ffb54730;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-chip {
      border-color: #ffb54738;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffb54714, #ffffff06);
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-chip__i {
      color: var(--smx-amber);
    }

    .smx-signal-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.45rem;
      margin-top: 1.2rem;
      color: #aaa6b7;
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      font-size: 0.67rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      line-height: 1.4;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .smx-signal-row__led {
      width: 0.45rem;
      height: 0.45rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--smx-oxide);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #ff3f691c, 0 0 1rem #ff3f6980;
    }

    .smx-signal-row__key {
      color: #f3f1f8;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .smx-signal-row__sep {
      color: #5b566a;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card {
      margin-top: 1.35rem;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid #ffb54738;
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff0b, #ffffff03), #05030ecc;
      box-shadow: inset 0 1px #ffffff0a, 0 1rem 2.5rem #00000026;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__top,
    .smx-lobby-card__foot {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      padding: 0.75rem 0.95rem;
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      line-height: 1.4;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__top {
      justify-content: space-between;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #ffffff12;
    }

    .smx-terminal-label {
      color: #f3f1f8;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__badge {
      color: var(--smx-amber);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__cell {
      min-height: 7.25rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      border-right: 1px solid #ffffff12;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__cell:last-child {
      border-right: 0;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__cell > span,
    .smx-route-node__tag {
      color: #a39eaf;
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__cell strong {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__cell small {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.45rem;
      color: #9894a6;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__foot {
      border-top: 1px solid #ffffff12;
      color: #aaa6b7;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: none;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__pulse {
      width: 0.42rem;
      height: 0.42rem;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--smx-cyan);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #00d4ff14, 0 0 0.9rem #00d4ff80;
    }

    .smx-lobby-card__foot strong {
      margin-left: auto;
      color: var(--smx-cyan);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    .smx-route-map {
      margin: 1.4rem 0 1.9rem;
      padding: 1rem;
      border: 1px solid #00d4ff2e;
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00d4ff0d, #ffffff04 48%, #ff3f6908);
    }

    .smx-route-map__head {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      padding: 0 0.2rem;
    }

    .smx-route-map__label {
      color: var(--smx-cyan);
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .smx-route-map__note {
      color: #928ea0;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
    }

    .smx-route-map__track {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      margin-top: 0.9rem;
    }

    .smx-route-node {
      min-height: 8.4rem;
      padding: 0.95rem;
      border: 1px solid #ffffff18;
      border-radius: 0.8rem;
      background: #05030eb8;
    }

    .smx-route-node--source {
      border-color: #ffb54750;
    }

    .smx-route-node--source .smx-route-node__tag {
      color: var(--smx-amber);
    }

    .smx-route-node--desk {
      border-color: #00d4ff50;
    }

    .smx-route-node--desk .smx-route-node__tag {
      color: var(--smx-cyan);
    }

    .smx-route-node--view {
      border-color: #ff3f6950;
    }

    .smx-route-node--view .smx-route-node__tag {
      color: #ff8ca4;
    }

    .smx-route-node h3 {
      margin: 0.55rem 0 0.35rem;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 1.04rem;
    }

    .smx-route-node p {
      margin: 0;
      color: #aaa6b7;
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .smx-route-arrow {
      display: flex;
      position: relative;
      min-width: 4.9rem;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      color: #8d899c;
      font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
      font-size: 0.58rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      line-height: 1.35;
      text-align: center;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .smx-route-arrow::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      height: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ffb54780, #00d4ff80, #ff3f6980);
    }

    .smx-route-arrow span {
      position: relative;
      padding: 0 0.25rem;
      background: #0a0612;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      border-color: #ffb54724;
      background: linear-gradient(110deg, #ffb5470a, #ffffff03 45%);
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 0;
      width: 3px;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--smx-amber), var(--smx-oxide));
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step:nth-child(2)::before {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--smx-cyan), #6f7cff);
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step:nth-child(3)::before {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ff8ca4, var(--smx-oxide));
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step:nth-child(4)::before {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #b38cff, var(--smx-cyan));
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .smx-setup-steps .gx-step__num {
      background: var(--smx-amber);
      box-shadow: 0 0 1.25rem #ffb54742;
      color: #140d05;
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-spec {
      border-color: #ffb54724;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffb5470d, #ffffff04);
    }

    .smx-guide-refresh .gx-spec__v {
      color: #ffd58e;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .smx-guide-refresh .smx-hero {
        padding: 1.25rem;
      }

      .smx-lobby-card__top,
      .smx-lobby-card__foot {
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      .smx-lobby-card__grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .smx-lobby-card__cell {
        min-height: 0;
        border-right: 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #ffffff12;
      }

      .smx-lobby-card__cell:last-child {
        border-bottom: 0;
      }

      .smx-lobby-card__foot strong {
        margin-left: 0;
      }

      .smx-route-map__track {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .smx-route-arrow {
        min-width: 0;
        min-height: 1.2rem;
        justify-content: flex-start;
        padding-left: 0.75rem;
        text-align: left;
      }

      .smx-route-arrow::before {
        position: static;
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 1px;
        height: 1rem;
        margin-right: 0.6rem;
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, #00d4ff80, #ff3f6980);
      }
    }
  </style>
</GuideLayout>
